From 9f68d00115a5e141ea4279d5e1db8113bdae524a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cary Palmer <24235924+professorpalmer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:40:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 51/52] cuda: chunked flash attention for prefill at depth
 (GGML_CUDA_FA_CHUNK=C, off by default)

Prefill-sized attention ops (at least GGML_CUDA_FA_PREFILL_F16_MIN_Q queries) over a quantized
K/V cache longer than C cells run the KV dimension in chunks of C cells (multiple of 256). Per
chunk: copy the chunk's K/V bytes into VRAM when they reach the host part of a tiered buffer
(copy engine, one copy per run), convert the chunk to f16 in pool memory sized by C, and run the
f16 tensor-core kernel with the chunk's mask columns (f16 or packed I32). The kernel gives each
output tile to one block and takes the needs_fixup path: unnormalized output and (max, rowsum)
per row. flash_attn_chunk_fold folds each chunk into a running result in dst; the last chunk
divides by the row sum. Memory per chunk does not depend on the KV length.

Chunked ops skip the whole-op staging and stay out of the tier prefetch pipeline. Sinks, ALiBi,
softcap, V as a view of K, several sequences, KV not a multiple of 256 and f16 K/V take the
normal path. Unset or 0: nothing changes.
